indiatimes.com/india/isros-gslv-f18/nvs-03-mission-successful-next-generation-navigation-satellite-placed-in-orbit-navic-constellation-gets-a-boost/articleshow/135374721.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135374721.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[GSLV-F18 carrying 2,250kg next-generation navigation satellite -- NVS-03 -- lifted off from the second launch pad at the Satish Dhawan Space Centre (SDSC-SHAR) in Sriharikota at 11.51pm on Friday, as scheduled. Around 18 minutes later, NVS-03 satellite was placed in a geosynchronous transfer orbit (GTO) of 37,023km apogee and 170km perigee.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/isros-gslv-f18/nvs-03-mission-successful-next-generation-navigation-satellite-placed-in-orbit-navic-constellation-gets-a-boost/articleshow/135374721.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/isros-gslv-f18/nvs-03-mission-successful-next-generation-navigation-satellite-placed-in-orbit-navic-constellation-gets-a-boost/articleshow/135374721.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-31T00:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">U Tejonmayam</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135376098,imgsize-35470.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Global South bears burden': At G20 meet, Jaishankar flags attacks on ships &amp; Indian seafarers in Hormuz]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-south-bears-burden-at-g20-meet-jaishankar-flags-attacks-on-ships-indian-seafarers-in-hormuz/articleshow/135373502.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135373502.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-south-bears-burden-at-g20-meet-j